        "title": "Microsoft cloud outlook · Execution is the gate",
        "html": "<style>body{margin:0;background:#f2f5f8;color:#193047;font-family:Arial,sans-serif}*{box-sizing:border-box}.wrap{padding:36px}.kicker{font-size:15px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1.2px;color:#56718a}h1{font-size:36px;font-weight:750;margin:10px 0}h2{font-size:21px;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 14px}.sub{font-size:20px;color:#4a6075;margin-bottom:24px}.panel{background:white;border:1px solid #dce4ec;border-radius:12px;padding:22px;height:100%}.table{font-size:17px;margin:0}.table td{padding:9px 6px;border-color:#e7edf2}.tag{display:inline-block;background:#e7f2fa;color:#17659b;border-radius:5px;padding:5px 9px;font-size:14px;margin-bottom:12px}.forecast{background:#fff3da;color:#866018}.logic{background:#193047;color:white;border-radius:12px;padding:22px;margin-top:24px}.logic p{font-size:19px;margin:0;line-height:1.5}.watch{font-size:17px;line-height:1.5;margin:0;padding-left:20px}.foot{font-size:14px;color:#64778a;margin-top:20px;line-height:1.5}</style><div class='wrap'><div class='kicker'>Microsoft FY27 Q1 · Investor outlook</div><h1>Cloud growth: execution is the gate</h1><div class='sub'>Strong reported growth and ambitious guidance, with demand still exceeding supply.</div><div class='row g-4'><div class='col-6'><div class='panel'><span class='tag'>ACTUALS · QUARTER ENDED SEPTEMBER 30</span><h2>Growth with heavy investment</h2><table class='table'><tr><td>Revenue</td><td><b>$92.3bn</b> · +19% YoY</td></tr><tr><td>Operating income / margin</td><td><b>$45.9bn</b> · +21% / 50%</td></tr><tr><td>Microsoft Cloud</td><td><b>$63.9bn</b> · +30%</td></tr><tr><td>Azure growth</td><td><b>48%</b></td></tr><tr><td>Commercial RPO</td><td><b>$677bn</b> · +73%</td></tr><tr><td>Capex</td><td><b>$45.2bn</b> · ~¾ CPUs/GPU-led short-lived assets</td></tr><tr><td>Operating / free cash flow</td><td><b>$58bn / $18.6bn</b></td></tr></table></div></div><div class='col-6'><div class='panel'><span class='tag forecast'>GUIDANCE · NOT COMPLETED RESULTS</span><h2>December-quarter expectations</h2><table class='table'><tr><td>Revenue / growth</td><td><b>$96–97.1bn</b> / 18–19%</td></tr><tr><td>Azure growth</td><td><b>49–50%</b> · constant currency</td></tr><tr><td>Cloud gross margin</td><td><b>~65%</b></td></tr><tr><td>Company operating margin</td><td>Slightly down YoY</td></tr><tr><td>Q2 capex</td><td><b>&gt;$50bn</b></td></tr><tr><td>Calendar-year capex</td><td><b>~$170bn</b></td></tr><tr><td>FY2027 free cash flow</td><td>Expected to remain positive</td></tr></table></div></div></div><div class='logic'><h2>Q&A synthesis · Capacity creates value across the stack</h2><p><b>Nadella:</b> a fungible pool supports Azure economics and Fabric, Foundry and Copilot through efficient operation, demand allocation and stack reinforcement.<br><b>Hood:</b> application-to-hardware efficiencies increased Foundry capacity in the reported quarter; further engineering gains remain a forecast dependency.</p></div><div class='row g-4 mt-0'><div class='col-6'><div class='panel'><h2>Delivery risks</h2><ul class='watch'><li>Some third-party GPU capacity shifted to the second half.</li><li>Token pricing and delayed capacity add uncertainty.</li><li>Demand conversion and engineering efficiency determine delivery.</li></ul></div></div><div class='col-6'><div class='panel'><h2>Investor monitoring priorities</h2><ul class='watch'><li>Track incremental capacity and fleet monetization.</li><li>Assess pricing and utilization alongside higher-layer value.</li><li>Watch cash-flow resilience as capital spending rises.</li></ul><div style='font-size:13px;color:#64778a;margin-top:8px'>Analytical watchlist, not assigned actions or company commitments.</div></div></div></div><div class='foot'>Source stated by speaker: October 28, 2026 investor call. Expectations are as of that date. Actual Azure growth has no currency basis specified in the lecture; the guidance is explicitly constant currency, so the two are not a like-for-like acceleration measure.</div></div>"
      }
